<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Prisoner of Conscience</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;In a moment of chance, Catra captures Adora during the Battle of Brightmoon, forcing her team to make a life-changing decision.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Will the former cadets be able to find themselves and rebuild what they lost?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A canon divergent fic, in which Catra and Adora had grown up closer to Lonnie, Kyle and Rogelio. Leaving Catra less isolated after Adoraâ€™s defection and forging them into one of Hordeâ€™s most elite units. As a result, Catra doesnâ€™t try to flee to the Crystal Castle and never â€˜lets goâ€™ of Adora. All whilst an increasingly desperate Shadow Weaver clings to power as Hordakâ€™s right hand.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>raywri</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
      <dc:subject>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>Fanworks</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Teen And Up Audiences</rdf:li>
